text:
maria: Quick heads-up — the mini Next + LlamaIndex starter we're using in the onboarding has two DX issues: telemetry not firing and Node SDK retry behavior diverging from Python. onboarding demos look flaky.

chris: Seen the telemetry gap before. Can you paste a tiny repro?

maria: Sure — minimal API handler:
```js
// pages/api/generate.js
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood();
export default async (req, res) => {
  const out = await client.chat.create({ model: 'redwood/open-alpha', messages: [{role:'user',content:'hi'}] });
  res.json(out);
};
```
In local dev the starter never shows events in Console unless I set REDWOOD_TELEMETRY=true. Docs say telemetry should be opt-out, not opt-in.

chris: That explains the missing header. For retries — what's the symptom?

maria: When the load spikes the Node sample surfaces 429 errors directly to the UI. The Python sample auto-retries with backoff so users don't notice. Onboarding QA hit this and it looked like a service outage.

julien: I started a small change to align node retry policy with python. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/rw-js/pull/542 :eyes: Needs unit + integ tests.

sam: Also noticed the LlamaIndex example in the starter and the eval harness use different tokenizers which changes eval scores ~7%. We should pin tokenizer and seed in the sample.

maria: Workaround for now: set env vars locally: REDWOOD_TELEMETRY=true and REDWOOD_RETRY_STRATEGY=exponential. But we need the starter to be correct out-of-the-box.

dev-bot: CI | tests failed for devex/mini-starters on node 18 — flakey timeout in tests/generate.test.js (job 7241)

chris: I'll add an integration test that simulates a burst of 429s and asserts retry+backoff behavior. Also will add a short note to the starter README about telemetry defaults until we patch.

julien: If my PR lands I'll push a PR to the starter repo that updates the SDK pin and adds the README note + CI test.

maria: Filing issue for the starter repo so we don't lose this: https://github.com/redwood-inference/devex/issues/88 — tagging @onboarding-team to update quickstart video if we change defaults.

sam: Suggestion: include a tiny eval script in the starter: `scripts/eval_local.py --seed 42 --tokenizer=gpt2` and a one-liner to pin quantization/kv-cache settings for reproducible local runs.

maria: Great, thanks all. I'll paste PR links here as things land and follow up with a short blurb for the onboarding doc. :thumbsup:
